  "headline": "Paradise on Earth",
  "short_description": "Srinagar, on the shores of Dal Lake, is known for houseboats, Mughal gardens and the natural beauty of the Kashmir Valley.",
  "about": "The summer capital of Jammu and Kashmir, Srinagar is famed for Dal Lake's houseboats and shikaras, Mughal-era gardens, and as a gateway to wider Kashmir.\n\nLocated in the Kashmir Valley of the Himalayas, around Dal Lake and the Jhelum river, at roughly 1,600 m elevation.\n\nKnown for Kashmiri handicrafts — pashmina shawls, carpets, paper-mâché and walnut wood carving — and Sufi-influenced traditions.\n\nPredominantly Muslim, with historic Hindu and Sikh shrines also present in the valley.",
  "history": "Founded over 2,000 years ago and later developed extensively under the Mughal emperors, who built the famous terraced gardens around Dal Lake.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Srinagar International Airport (airport)\n- Srinagar Railway Station (railway)\n- Srinagar TRC Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
